      "guid": "com.brosheff.persistentfir",
      "name": "PersistentFiR",
      "slug": "persistentfir",
      "teaser": "Prevents FiR status from being stripped just for entering a raid.",
      "thumbnail": "",
      "downloads": 1385,
      "favourites_count": 12,
      "description": "<p>Persistent FiR preserves the Found in Raid status of FiR items in your inventory when you enter a raid with them.</p>\n<p>I made this mod because I enjoy playing with the Vagabond mod. In that setup, even if I found a specific FiR item needed for a quest, extracting to the Hideout could effectively make that item unusable for the normal quest or trader progression flow. This was because I had to play at least one more raid before I could access traders again. I felt this created an unintended balance conflict with the existing game systems, so I made this mod to address that issue.</p>\n<p>Vagabond is not required. If you have ever accidentally brought a FiR item into a raid and lost the ability to sell it on the flea market, this mod may be useful for you.</p>\n<p>This mod prevents FiR status from being removed simply because an item was brought into a raid.</p>\n<p>It does not change FiR loss caused by Run Through, death, or other normal raid failure conditions.</p>\n",
      "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2793/persistentfir",
